From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: postmarketOS <info@postmarketos.org>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] serial: samsung: log Bluejay Bluetooth UART state

Log the hardware state before shutdown to diagnose a BCM4389 controller
which accepts transmitted bytes but never returns an HCI event.
---
 drivers/tty/serial/samsung_tty.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/samsung_tty.c b/drivers/tty/serial/samsung_tty.c
index 666666666666..777777777777 100644
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/samsung_tty.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/samsung_tty.c
@@ -1171,6 +1171,13 @@ static void s3c64xx_serial_shutdown(struct uart_port *port)
 {
 	struct s3c24xx_uart_port *ourport = to_ourport(port);
 
+	if (port->mapbase == 0x175b0000)
+		dev_info(port->dev,
+			 "BT UART close: UTRSTAT=%08x UFSTAT=%08x UINTP=%08x UINTM=%08x\n",
+			 rd_regl(port, S3C2410_UTRSTAT),
+			 rd_regl(port, S3C2410_UFSTAT),
+			 rd_regl(port, S3C64XX_UINTP), rd_regl(port, S3C64XX_UINTM));
+
 	ourport->tx_enabled = 0;
 	ourport->tx_mode = 0;
 	ourport->rx_enabled = 0;
-- 
2.51.0
